{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "$id": "urn:synapsecommand:hla:local:1:demo",
  "title": "synapse-hla demo manifest",
  "description": "DIR/demo.json (OPS-13, OPS-18, OPS-01, D-14, CR-L03, CR-L04, R38, R39). BLOCKED when the worker, rtinode or the synthetic publisher is missing: the missing items, the FOM digests checked against the pins, no source commit, external_customer_interoperability NOT_TESTED. PASS or FAIL when the exercise ran: the evidence class (development evidence on any build of this round), the tested reference and the scope statement of R39, the profile declaration bundled-fom-created, the pinned FOM digests, rtinode's address, port, process id and every start attempt, the runs main and no-time (configuration digest, federation name, the module digests the publisher reported for the bytes that created the federation, its process ids, every barrier step with the capture seq that showed it, the refresh reflections, the session summary, the capture digest, the replay, every semantic checkpoint in its fixed order or none), the clean-up (every process started, reaped, and the port released) and the failures (their stage, a fixed reason; a publisher failure only in the publisher's own vocabulary). A clean-up PASS needs every process reaped and the port not left open. PASS only when both runs pass every checkpoint, nothing failed and nothing was left behind: in each run the publisher reported its module digests and GroundVehicle as the class it registered at, created and destroyed its federation, reported no failure and exited 0, every one of the seven steps was acknowledged, the session is COMPLETE, the capture has its digest and the replay is COMPLETE; rtinode has its pid and port after exactly one listening start. The seven steps of a run are R38's, each at its fixed position with its barrier number, event and tag (review finding R8-r2-F1). Not expressible here and held by the code and its tests instead: that rtinode's pid and port are those of its listening start, that the module digests the publisher reported equal fom_sha256 (else the run fails with E_DEPENDENCY_PIN), and that the step seqs rise.",
